new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d7f54bd7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc-build/md064.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+This rule is triggered when the destination of a link or image uses a URL
+scheme that is not in the `allowed_schemes` parameter (for example, with
+`allowed_schemes` set to `["https"]`):
+
+```markdown
+[Download](ftp://example.com/file.zip)
+
+<http://example.com>
+
+[reference]: http://example.com
+```
+
+To fix this, use an allowed scheme:
+
+```markdown
+[Download](https://example.com/file.zip)
+
+<https://example.com>
+
+[reference]: https://example.com
+```
+
+The destinations of inline links and images, link reference definitions and
+autolinks are checked; bare URLs in text are not. Destinations without a scheme
+(relative paths, fragments) are never reported, and schemes are compared
+without regard to case.
+
+Note: With the default empty value of `allowed_schemes`, every scheme is
+allowed and this rule never reports a violation.
+
+Rationale: Some URL schemes are insecure or unsupported where the document is
+published (for example, `http:` instead of `https:`, or `javascript:`).
